  partName: Intake Runner (3)
  description: The Intake Runner (3) is a large, complex metal component situated
    at the middle-center-front of the jet engine, responsible for channeling air-fuel
    mixture from the intake manifold to the engine's combustion chambers. Its metal-mid
    material provides a balance of strength, durability, and thermal resistance,
    making it suitable for this application. Interestingly, the intake runner's front
    location allows for optimal airflow and minimal pressure losses.
